window.products.push({"id":864108,"name":"Wilton Armetale William and Mary Trivet, Round, 7-1/2-Inch","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51QWQBCK3SL._AC_.jpg","description":"Product Description WILTON ARMETALE offers a creative way to cook and serve every day. This intricately designed Trivet is part of our popular William and Mary collection. Based on the coat-of-arms of William III and Queen Mary, this intricate, baroque-inspired design adds a sense of grandeur to the table. All of our pieces are designed for both decorative and practical use making them appropriate for parties, dinners or simply everyday use. Constructed of 100% recycled food-safe aluminum based alloy, Wilton Armetale cookware and serveware will not rust, crack, chip, dent, or tarnish. Bring our pieces straight to the table for an attractive presentation that keeps food hotter longer. Our metal has been independently tested and approved for both cooking and serving food. Our serving pieces can also be pre-chilled to use for condiments, cheeses, crudités, dips, and more. Unit measures 7-1/2-inch by 1-inch. To clean, hand wash with hot soapy water and towel dry. Do not put in the microwave or dishwasher. With proper care your Armetale treasures can last a lifetime. A family-owned company since 1892, Wilton Armetale offers a vast array of cookware and serveware designed to capture the spirit of your life. Amazon.com Since 1892, Wilton Armetale has constructed unique serving pieces in silver and pewter, gracefully combining beauty and durability. Individually handcrafted in Lancaster, Pennsylvania, no two pieces are exactly alike. Non-toxic metal ensures the safety of all food items, and effectively keeps a side dish or main course at the desired temperature. Wilton Armetale guarantees that under normal circumstances, serveware pieces will not rust, tarnish, crack, chip, or dent. Based upon the coat-of-arms of William III and Queen Mary, this intricate, baroque-inspired design adds a sense of grandeur to the table. Elaborate scrollwork, meandering vines, and interwoven flowers are opulently sculpted in low relief, adding a sense of regal dignity. Measuring 7-3/4 inches in diameter, the detailed pattern covers the entire face of the trivet, while a cut out in the shape of a circle adorns the center. Resting on four plastic coated feet, the trivet can hold a substantial serving piece while simultaneously protecting delicate tables. For best results, Wilton Armetale recommends washing all serving pieces by hand, and instructs users not to place them in the microwave or dishwasher. --Lea Werbel","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51QWQBCK3SL._AC_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Wilton Armetale","source_asin":"B0000TR748","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-864108","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0000TR748","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B0000TR748","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
